(reached BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT via 4308 -> 1684 -> 1692), a pervasive DGROUP base-loss (same class as
patches 163/164 for its neighbours 1996/19b9).  ES=DS=DGROUP; the model-record base is
mrec = word[DGROUP:(word[DGROUP:0x2674])+0x27f4] (asm 16be) and the descriptor near-offset is
di = word[DGROUP:(mrec+0x20)] (16c9); the es:[6]->es:[8] copy at 16e3 is a loaded-SEGMENT window, not
DGROUP:c006/c008.  Ghidra typed DAT_1000_e674 int** and rendered mrec as DAT_1000_e674[0x13fa]
(0x27f4/2 scaling) -> a wild host dereference (SIGSEGV, gdb-confirmed at FUN_0000_1692+231; the
deterministic-from-repo-root crash after the `[ext] op 0x4c` display-list commands, pinned via the
core-dump loop).  All rebuilt offsets are 16-bit -> in-bounds; the fill/broadcast logic is otherwise
instruction-faithful (verified vs asm 0x16be..0x1718).  Behaviour-neutral for verify (model-loader
path, unreached by the 19 flows).

